preConditionHook:
// Trend from the open, as a per-session flag. Set to +1 the first time a bar
// closes above the session's first bar's high, to -1 the first time one
// closes below its low, and cleared back to 0 if price later closes through
// the other extreme of that same first bar. The flag is reset at every
// session start, so it never leaks across days.
//
// Brooks's glossary form -- a trend beginning at one of the first bars whose
// start REMAINS one of the day's extremes -- needs a no-pullback counter, a
// session-extreme tracker and a persistence test. The chapter's own
// mechanical proxy is what is coded here: as soon as a bar closes beyond the
// first bar's extreme the day is a trend-from-the-open day in that direction,
// at least for that moment. The strict form's extra content is carried by
// SessionExtremeSetInOpeningWindow.
//
// ORDER OF THE FOUR TESTS is safe as written: firstLow <= firstHigh, so a
// close cannot be both above firstHigh and below firstLow, and no bar can set
// and later clear the flag in the same pass.
//
// SESSION MODEL, per the standing decision: the twin's date > date[1],
// mirrored as day_of(ctx.Time(0)) > day_of(ctx.Time(1)) on integer day
// serials. tfo holds only the exact small integers 0, 1 and -1, so the
// conditions compare it through el_eq for the twin's spelling even though no
// tolerance can change the outcome. Intraday bars only.
if (day_of(ctx.Time(0)) > day_of(ctx.Time(1))) {
    tfo = 0;
    firstHigh = high[0];
    firstLow = low[0];
} else {
    if (tfo == 0 && el_gt(close[0], firstHigh)) tfo = 1;
    if (tfo == 0 && el_lt(close[0], firstLow)) tfo = -1;
    if (tfo == 1 && el_lt(close[0], firstLow)) tfo = 0;
    if (tfo == -1 && el_gt(close[0], firstHigh)) tfo = 0;
}
